<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__0467__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. SCHWEINFURTH GREEN" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Asphalt or Bitumen used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. SCHWEINFURTH GREEN"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Stains of pitch, varnish, or oil paint, which have become dry, must first be softened with a little fresh butter or lard, and then treated with the powder of the scouring ball."@en ;
